==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
*1 [[Formicidaean Ariant]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns once 100 Cat Units have been defeated.
*1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns once 200 Cat Units have been defeated.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**4 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]]s spawn, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage has a lot of Mini Angel Cyclones, so make sure to bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] because they can push hard and make it difficult to reach Lowkey. The best option for the Formicidaean Ariants is to use [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. As for the Imperator Saels, a combination of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] to [[Freeze]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to chip them down works well. Lowkey can be easily dealt with by either [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]. The latter prevents your Ramen Cats from getting cursed.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo juggles the Mini Angel Cyclone easily. A swarm of them can melt the cyclones in mere seconds.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Luna targets 3/5 enemies on this stage and has Zombie Killer, due to this, she can be a steady source of DPS, especially against the boss, Lowkey.
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: Dioramos can Knockback and Slow both the Imperator Saels and Mini Angel Cyclones, combined with their naturally high DPS and bulk, they are a spectacular choice for this stage.

==Trivia==
*Crag of Monte Cristo's Japanese name, Gankustuou (顔窟王, "Face Cave King"), sounds identical to ''Gankustuou'' (巌窟王, "Cavern King"), the Japanese title of the novel [[wikipedia:The Count of Monte Cristo|''The Count of Monte Cristo'']] and its [[wikipedia:Gankutsuou: The Count of Monte Cristo|anime adaptation]]. The joke is that instead of spelling ''Gan'' as 巌 like the novel and anime, the stage uses the kanji 顔, meaning "[[Lowkey|face]]".

